  "readme": [
    {
      "section": "@lemoncat7/dsh-web-search",
      "text": "Configurable web access for [DeepSeek Harness](https://github.com/deepseek-ai/deepseek-harness). The plugin provides DSH's native `web_search` and `web_fetch` tools: administrators select the search backend, while direct public-page retrieval uses the same plugin-scoped proxy and security boundary. A constrained `web_source` tool is also available when an agent must verify raw HTML markers or script-embedded data under an explicit source procedure; normal page reading remains the job of `web_fetch`."
    },
    {
      "section": "Compatibility",
      "text": "Supports DeepSeek Harness **0.2.1-rc.2** as the minimum, with **0.2.1-rc.5** build and regression verification, on Node.js **^22.19.0** or **>=24.0.0**. The host is still a release candidate. Desktop origin compatibility is covered by automated HTTP tests, not a real Desktop client run. See [compatibility](docs/dsh-021-compatibility.md) and the release notes for other host versions.\n\nSupported providers:"
    },
    {
      "section": "Compatibility",
      "text": "- SearXNG — self-hosted, keyless general web search\n- Wikipedia — keyless encyclopedia search; Simplified Chinese by default\n- Tavily — agent-oriented API search\n- Brave Search — traditional web and news search\n- Gemini Grounded Search — Google Search grounding and URL Context for queries containing a URL\n\nOnly the selected provider receives each query. The plugin does not silently fan out requests or spend quota on fallback services."
    },
    {
      "section": "Install",
      "text": "```bash\ndsh plugin --profile web add @lemoncat7/dsh-web-search\n```\n\nOpen **Settings → Plugins → Plugin configuration → Web search** to choose a provider, store API credentials, test the draft configuration, and save it without restarting DSH.\n\nThe default backend is keyless Chinese Wikipedia so a new installation can be verified immediately. Use SearXNG, Tavily, Brave, or Gemini for general web coverage."
    },
    {
      "section": "Local SearXNG",
      "text": "```bash\ndocker compose -f deploy/searxng/compose.yml up -d\ncurl -fsS -X POST http://127.0.0.1:8080/search -d 'q=DeepSeek&format=json'\n```\n\nThe included deployment binds to loopback only. Do not expose it publicly without authentication, rate limiting, and the controls recommended by SearXNG."
    },
    {
      "section": "Local SearXNG",
      "text": "The settings card can read general-purpose engines from the configured instance, probe them with bounded concurrency, sort successful engines by latency, and save a per-client engine selection. Failed or empty searches can be retried from zero to three times."
    },
    {
      "section": "Security",
      "text": "- Search JSON and fetched text are capped at 2 MiB; search responses are schema-validated.\n- `web_fetch` accepts credential-free public HTTP(S) URLs only and blocks loopback, private, link-local, and reserved destinations.\n- Fetch redirects are capped at five and every hop is revalidated. Binary bodies are rejected.\n- `web_source` applies the same fetch policy and supports only bounded range reads or a bounded set of exact source markers, with at most 120,000 returned characters.\n- API keys are resolved through DSH Credential Store and sent only in provider-defined authorization headers.\n- Browser settings routes enforce exact same-origin writes, cap request bodies, and never return secret values.\n- Fetch and source inspection are constrained read-only public-web capabilities, not internal-network access or arbitrary command execution."
    },
    {
      "section": "Proxy",
      "text": "Set `DSH_WEB_SEARCH_PROXY` to an absolute HTTP(S) proxy URL. Search and fetch share this dispatcher; it remains scoped to the plugin and does not change networking for model providers or other DSH plugins. Loopback and private IPv4 destinations bypass it for local search backends, while `web_fetch` independently rejects non-public destinations. Add custom direct hosts to the comma-separated `DSH_WEB_SEARCH_NO_PROXY` variable."
    },
    {
      "section": "Development",
      "text": "```bash\nnpm install\nnpm run check\n```"
    },
    {
      "section": "Attribution",
      "text": "Maintained as an MIT-licensed derivative of [zmh2000829/dsh-web-search-multi](https://github.com/zmh2000829/dsh-web-search-multi). The original license notice is retained."
    },
    {
